Also written ''bannerol.''

'''band-fish''' (band′fish), ''n.'' An English name of (''a'') the ''Cepola rubescens'', a species of the family ''Cepolidæ'', more specifically called ''red band-fish;'' (''b'') the oar-fish, ''Regalecus glesne.'' Also called ''snake-fish.''

'''bandful''' (band′fu̇l; by miners, bon′tl), ''n.'' [< ''band''<sup>2</sup> + ''-ful''<sup>2</sup>.] In ''coal-mining'', a load of men carried up or down in the mine by sitting on chain-loops attached to the hoisting-rope, as was customary before the introduction of the cage and man-engine. [S. Staffordshire, Eng.]

